{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1285637-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate","id":1285637,"title":"What do you want to see in Lunars: Fangs at the Gate?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-07T12:35:08-08:00","id":1285637,"title":"What do you want to see in Lunars: Fangs at the Gate?","content":"What do you want to see in Lunars: Fangs at the Gate? In terms of mechanics, thematics, lore, and whatever else interests you, what do you want to get out of Lunars?<br /> <br /> Please, be as specific as possible. I think that it could be interesting to compare hopes and expectations to the material and reactions once things start to be released.<br /> <br /> As for me: what I want is to be able to rebuild my favorite RPG character, a monkey-totem lunar martial artists (unabashedly inspired by the aesthetics of DBZ). 2E Lunars were mechanically fraught, to be sure, but the combination of DBT (SSJ4 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />), Relentless Lunar Fury (and the fury keyword system, which I quite enjoyed), attribute charms, and martial arts was a ton of fun. Obviously, the character would be mechanically quite different in a 3E incarnation, but if I can recapture the feel of how that character worked, I will likely be quite happy overall with Lunars.<br /> <br /> (Bonus: if Lunars also doesn't make the Realm seem even more randomly evil and totally ineffectual, I will be impressed as well as happy!)<br /> <br /> So, what do you want out of Lunars: Fangs at the Gate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T13:21:36-08:00","id":1285661,"title":"","content":"I want to see lots of canonical Lunar &quot;Half-Castes&quot;; the Moon-Touched. Previous editions have always given Lunar rulers beastmen followers, but have rather shied away from those who also (or only) inherited the less-physical, more-magical gifts of the Lunar Exalted.<br /> <br /> I also want to see God-Blooded princes and princesses, born of romantic or political unions with mighty spirits; Elementals, terrestrial gods, stray Celestial gods, demons, Fair Folk, anything.<br /> <br /> These magical children would never stand a chance against Dragon-Blooded, but they would more useful agents than mere mortals.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also want to see a lot more sorcerous workings used on peoples, territories, edifices, and tools passed down among mortals, as Lunar Exalted make use of Terrestrial and Celestial sorcery to bolster the power of their holdings and followers, with none of the Realm\u2019s distrust of the art.<br /> <br /> Full Moon kings who never become sorcerers can trade favors across the Silver Pact to acquire the services of Celestial sorcerers.<br /> <br /> Halta is cute, with people living in trees with talking animals, but that really seems to be only scratching the surface of the kind of fantasy societies and enchanted environments that Lunars could create which are inimical and resistant to invasion or assimilation by the Realm, Lookshy, or Prasad.<br /> <br /> \u201cI have ensorcelled the land to produce bountiful crops, but even if you take it from my people, good luck maintaining the blessing without performing the spiritual rites which would blaspheme your phony religion!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, you turned my transformed people against me? Will you still enjoy their loyalty after following the rites of the Immaculate faith robs them of the strength I gave them within a generation?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Whether by inheritance, Charms, or simply sorcerous workings, the Lunar Exalted will not lack for methods to make their progeny and followers super-human, to varying degrees proportionate to the rarity and importance of the minion.<br /> <br /> The question isn\u2019t the how or the why, and all of the most impressive methods won\u2019t be available until at least Essence 3, anyway.<br /> <br /> The question is whether or not Third Edition will actually deliver on them, as past Editions never did. <br /> <br /> The fact that the core book bothered to tell us more about Yena\u2019s Daughters than directly about Yena Bone-Breaker herself is promising. It showed us that a Lunar\u2019s children can be heroes themselves; political actors who go out, do things, make names for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T13:26:45-08:00","id":1285663,"title":"","content":"<b>Animals:</b><br /> <br /> 1) Thunder Lizard (brontosaurus)<br /> 2) Terror Wing (pterodactyl)<br /> 3) Giant Octopus/Squid<br /> 5) Whale<br /> 6) Dolphin<br /> 7) Giant Spider<br /> 8) Mountain Goat<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sorcerous Initiations:</b><br /> <br /> 1) Song-casting, spell-singing<br /> <br /> 2) Seasonal cycles, day/night cycles, lunar cycles, cooperation from two assistants in different stages of life than you (maiden, mother, crone / son, father, grandfather)<br /> <br /> 3) In the vein of &quot;Pact with an Ifrit Lord&quot;, &quot;Mentored by a Forge-God&quot;, because maybe I'd like to play <i>League of Legends'</i> Ornn as a Mountain Goat Lunar, and I imagine plenty of Solar players would appreciate an initiation that helps with crafting","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T13:39:20-08:00","id":1285671,"title":"","content":"Shapeshifting and animal stuff as a facet of a larger whole rather than the central focus of their powers; ideally mystical \u2018outsider\u2019 types, representing what is untamed and unknown rather than animal Exalted. Err, honestly I\u2019m curious to see how the excellency pans out\u2014 don\u2019t love the core book version where you can arbitrarily have a solar dice-cap provided you perform cursory stunts. Chiefly because this sort of trivializes stunting and makes it \u2018mandatory\u2019 rather than something engaged in chiefly for a more enjoyable game experience. I\u2019m sure the authors will handle it neatly (was impressed by the terrestrial one). Less body horror\u2014 I hope than previous editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T13:58:07-08:00","id":1285675,"title":"","content":"Well, firstly good mechanics, obviously. But I think everyone's going to say that.<br /> <br /> Political factions that actually make sense (probably by being regional rather than about what Lunars should even be doing).<br /> Mechanics that aren't too complicated.<br /> Charms that let you <i>do</i> stuff, not just be better at stuff you can already do.<br /> No Moon charms that are as powerful and interesting as Full Moon and Changing Moon charms.<br /> A No Moon anima banner that's actually good.<br /> Casteless mechanically written in a way where the authors recognise that Casteless are often going to be played temporarily before getting a Caste.<br /> Sorcerous initiations that are nice and bizarre.<br /> Plenty of Celestial Spells (there's already plenty of Terrestrial spells).<br /> Moonsilver Tattoos that look unique, rather than the same as every other Lunar's.<br /> Charms for shamanism. Charms for trickery. Charms for body horror and mutation. Charms that let you lead packs of animals.<br /> Essence 2+ charms that are in no way copies of Solar charms, let alone underpowered copies. (Essence 1 charms are fine. I've no problem with Lunars using Ox-Body, Monkey Leap and Graceful Crane. As long as they're not weakened versions.)<br /> Examples of really weird barbarian societies that have been moulded by Lunars. Beastmen, sure, but more than that. It's no good if it's just Frog-person Nexus.<br /> Lunars actually straight-up ruling really weird barbarian societies.<br /> Lunar ancients who are obsessed with things that are not Solars.<br /> A Lunar history section that tells you what they did in the Shogunate, and it's not &quot;they hid in the Wyld.&quot;<br /> Craft charms that are actually fun, not just more dice/craft xp/slots.<br /> A Silver Pact that is genuinely shocked the Solars have returned, rather than having spent ages acting as if the Solars would soon return.<br /> Some kind of advantage for practicing an Animal Style rather than other styles.<br /> An excellency not based on stunting. Or in fact, any charms based on stunting.<br /> <br /> I actually expect to get most of these... except the last two. But you can't win them all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-07-2019, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T14:01:10-08:00","id":1285681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Giant Octopus/Squid</div> </div> </div> </div>There's already stats for a Kraken.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me. I want Lunars to be able to turn into giant versions of their spirit shapes, and it actually be good. And be able to do it y Essence 3.<br /> You could do it in 2nd ed at Essence 5, but it was, frankly, rubbish. The bonuses you got were small enough that a Tyrant Lizard-sized spider was nowhere near as good as a Tyrant Lizard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T14:19:39-08:00","id":1285689,"title":"","content":"<b>Artifacts:</b><br /> <br /> Circe's sorcerous shepherd's-crook staff of transforming dudes into animals and bewitching their minds<br /> <br /> A 5-dot cauldron which allows a Lunar to brew magical potions and ointments that retain their potency only as long as the Lunar commits the motes but which allows the user to bestow blessings on others through Evocations that Exalted Charms generally can't provide, and serves as a sorcerous means for works of empowerment<br /> <br /> A bow that enchants an arrow to continue attacking the original target until it hits, as long as you continue to aim at that target. The better you get with it, the more an arrow can act on its own, like the Signature Air Thrown Charm, Persistent Hornet Attack.<br /> <br /> A bow that inspires great terror within anyone who sees you aiming at them (which can be used to effectively interrogate someone you catch with a Hold At Bay situation), which peaks when you shoot at them with a successful withering attack, and which you can use to inspire berserker rage if you score a decisive attack that fails to kill them.<br /> <br /> Lightning Torment Hatchets<br /> <br /> Gauntlets of Distant Prowess<br /> <br /> Ivy Valentine's chain-link whip-sword.<br /> <br /> A yoyo where the ball is a robotic spider with a venomous bite, and which can be used as a remote-controlled spy on the end of an ever-extending string.<br /> <br /> A shark-tooth sword that regenerates any teeth it loses, and which can behave like a chainsaw (which might be what costs it teeth in the first place).<br /> <br /> A grand goremaul that flows as you swing it, leaving behind most of its mass so that your strike is faster and more accurate, with all of the mass catching up after you hit to land the full force of the head, but if you miss the snap-back throws you off balance if you can't recover into another swing at your opponent.<br /> <br /> Spider-Man web-Shooters, either as bracelets or part of a whole-body suit which itself allows anyone to cling to walls (because Spider-Manning around becomes a lot more difficult if you can't cling to walls)<br /> <br /> Ant-Man's shrinking/growing body-suit.<br /> <br /> Death at the Root<br /> <br /> A moonsilver version of the Scabbard of the Living Weapon, but with graduated levels of power through Evocations, and not as broken<br /> <br /> The Bellerophon reins of Servant Rider (Medusa) from the Fate/Stay Night franchise; bridle, control, and enrage any beast for battle<br /> <br /> A shapeshifting robe that becomes any set of clothing you need for any social context or disguise<br /> <br /> Armor that works like the Warrior's &quot;Dragon's Body And Scales&quot; from <i>Dragon Marked For Death</i>, which can transform itself and its wearer to shield him and his allies against powerful, area-of-effect attacks, or transform his defense into offense to leave him vulnerable as he winds up for a single powerful strike.<br /> <br /> A firewand that works like the Empress' &quot;Dragon's Arms and Fangs&quot;, which works like razor claws and transforms for strong bites and fire-breath attacks.<br /> <br /> God-Kicking boots that work like the Shinobi's &quot;Dragon's Legs and Wings&quot;, which would be particularly dangerous with Swaying Grass Style, Centipede Style, and possibly Falcon Style.<br /> <br /> Armor that fuses with you and transforms you to mimic the spell Incomparable Body Armor<br /> <br /> Venom symbiote living armor","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T17:59:01-08:00","id":1285749,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see themes exploring the range of outsider to monstrosity. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T20:01:13-08:00","id":1285781,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1230119-exalted-mobile-homes\">Exalted mobile homes.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T20:49:21-08:00","id":1285786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1285637-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1285671#post1285671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shapeshifting and animal stuff as a facet of a larger whole rather than the central focus of their powers; ideally mystical \u2018outsider\u2019 types, representing what is untamed and unknown rather than animal Exalted. Err, honestly I\u2019m curious to see how the excellency pans out\u2014 don\u2019t love the core book version where you can arbitrarily have a solar dice-cap provided you perform cursory stunts. Chiefly because this sort of trivializes stunting and makes it \u2018mandatory\u2019 rather than something engaged in chiefly for a more enjoyable game experience. I\u2019m sure the authors will handle it neatly (was impressed by the terrestrial one). Less body horror\u2014 I hope than previous editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jive you\u2019re back! Welcome!!<br /> <br /> Yeah I am interested in them being more then just shapeshifting animal folks. I would like them to be more the Monsters and sacred beasts prowling the Hinterlands, like witches and wanderers. Sometimes beasts sometimes odd mystical folk hero\u2019s and tricksters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T22:14:14-08:00","id":1285804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1285637-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1285681#post1285681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's already stats for a Kraken.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me. I want Lunars to be able to turn into giant versions of their spirit shapes, and it actually be good. And be able to do it y Essence 3.<br /> You could do it in 2nd ed at Essence 5, but it was, frankly, rubbish. The bonuses you got were small enough that a Tyrant Lizard-sized spider was nowhere near as good as a Tyrant Lizard.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIrc, this was spoiled already. Getting Legendary Size is supposed to be an essence 1 thing, but it costs 4m per turn in combat/4m per hour out of combat, I think. In addition to any activation costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T22:18:38-08:00","id":1285805,"title":"","content":"Unison was in Arms already. It could totally become Venom type armor, I think. Not sentient or clingy necessarily, but it sounds like it becomes one with you. Sprouting weapons a la Incomparable Body Armor would also seem legit for it, I think.<br /> <br /> I think Circe's Staff will be much easier to build after we see what Lunar charms can do in regards to turning people into animals, whether or not it is in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 02-08-2019, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T22:38:51-08:00","id":1285808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1285637-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1285804#post1285804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IIrc, this was spoiled already. Getting Legendary Size is supposed to be an essence 1 thing, but it costs 4m per turn in combat/4m per hour out of combat, I think. In addition to any activation costs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, that's being able to tutn into Legendary Size creatures, like siege lizards and mammoths.<br /> <br /> I'm talking about being able to turn into a Legendary Size version of your sprit shape, and for its stats to rival mammoths, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T22:55:46-08:00","id":1285811,"title":"","content":"Rules and especially charms that let me play a terrifying shape-stealing monster Exalt with the power that implies. I want to play Lunars and feel like they are badass, powerful, and to understand why the Realm fears them so much. Not just feel like I'm playing &quot;weaker solars&quot;.<br /> I would also love to see how Lunars handle social influence different that Solars and DB's.<br /> <br /> <i>Oh, and I don't want every Lunar to be intimidating. But I want them to wield power that strikes fear in the hearts of an empire of ten-thousand dragon-blooded.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T23:51:21-08:00","id":1285823,"title":"","content":"Consistency with the previews?<br /> <br /> Something emotionally resonant enough to make me cry a bit would be a plus. Especially if it's in an Artifact (I swear, that Cathak family sword).<br /> <br /> I would be interested in seeing a character written up in a manner that completely shatters the previously designed image that I've long been attached to, which I end up liking better.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Really, the most important thing I want to see is something I don't know that I want until I see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 02-08-2019, 02:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T03:23:23-08:00","id":1285841,"title":"","content":"More Celestial Circle Sorcery stuff, not just spells but also workings. I'm also looking forward to seeing more Moonsilver artifacts, both because they are awesome and for inspiration on making my own. I'm also interested to see the less physical aspects of Lunar power; Full Moons shapeshifting into Tyrant Lizards and eating armies is all well and good, but I'm eager to see the more subtle aspects of what Changing and No Moons can do. Also, just more mechanics in general. I seem to be the one person in the universe that likes the Lunar Excellency presented in the core, but it'll be good to have all the Charms for making NPCs for my players to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13696-knurlurzhad","name":"Knurlurzhad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T04:49:07-08:00","id":1285850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1285637-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1285661#post1285661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to see lots of canonical Lunar &quot;Half-Castes&quot;; the Moon-Touched. Previous editions have always given Lunar rulers beastmen followers, but have rather shied away from those who also (or only) inherited the less-physical, more-magical gifts of the Lunar Exalted.<br /> <br /> I also want to see God-Blooded princes and princesses, born of romantic or political unions with mighty spirits; Elementals, terrestrial gods, stray Celestial gods, demons, Fair Folk, anything.<br /> <br /> These magical children would never stand a chance against Dragon-Blooded, but they would more useful agents than mere mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it all depends on how things will pan out for the &quot;children of the chosen&quot; as a whole when new fluff and mechanics on them do come up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T05:25:01-08:00","id":1285852,"title":"","content":"Lunars as cool and independent Exalted faction. Able to became real thing in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T05:40:17-08:00","id":1285854,"title":"","content":"Actually, I'd like to request a name change. If we could replace &quot;the&quot; with some word starting with N, we'd have a nice acronym &quot;FANG&quot;.<br /> <br /> While I do appreciate the meta humor of having &quot;Fangs At <i>Ni!</i> Gate&quot; it seems like a silly place anyway.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T06:03:52-08:00","id":1285859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1285637-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1285823#post1285823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consistency with the previews?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the previews have generally been good. If the book is exactly what I expect based on the previews, I'll likely consider it 9/10 (and 10/10 is very subjective of course).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really, the most important thing I want to see is something I don't know that I want until I see it. </div> </div> </div>This is one of the reasons I like Minton's writing of locations; he doesn't just rehash old stuff but fixed, the way forumites demand.<br /> He gives you entirely new cool societies and locations.<br /> That's why I liked Compass: the North more than any other compass. Scavenger Lands was mostly stuff from 1st ed, but in Compass: North, while the stuff from Bastions of the North was still there, there was a whole chapter of interesting new locations.<br /> <br /> The other thing is with charms. I want better, more interesting No Moon charms because I felt that my No Moon basically could mostly just take Sorcery, Tracking and Spirit-related stuff.<br /> But I don't really actually have a lot of ideas for cool, interesting No Moon charms.<br /> What I'm hoping is to see a whole bunch of Intelligence and Wits charms I'd never have thought of.<br /> <br /> Some of the No Moon charms shown so far are ones I'd expected; stuff like Echo-Drinking Awareness, History-Divining Scent, Moon Follows Sun Assurance.<br /> But others I'd never have thought of... yet in retrospect, they seem obvious. Of course there should be a charm to introduce a fact about a spirit. Of course there should be a charm to whip out an item and declare retrospectively you bought/stole/crafted* it earlier. But I didn't think of it until I saw it.<br /> <br /> *I like how &quot;Lunar&quot; it is too. The Solar equivalent is just for crafting, but Lunars are Wits Exalts, not Craft Exalts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T06:06:25-08:00","id":1285861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knurlurzhad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1285637-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1285841#post1285841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to be the one person in the universe that likes the Lunar Excellency presented in the core, but it'll be good to have all the Charms for making NPCs for my players to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I think most people like it. But they said &quot;huh, that's cool&quot;, and moved on, whereas those of us who don't like it keep bringing it up (especially as, for me, everything else is good so far and that's the one bit I don't like).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T08:21:54-08:00","id":1285900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1285637-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1285805#post1285805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unison was in Arms already. It could totally become Venom type armor, I think. Not sentient or clingy necessarily, but it sounds like it becomes one with you. Sprouting weapons a la Incomparable Body Armor would also seem legit for it, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Venom Symbiotes don't turn into heavy armor or enable Perfect Soak; they extrude webs or tentacles for mobility and ranged attacks, and change appearance for disguise/camouflage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1285637-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1285808#post1285808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, that's being able to tutn into Legendary Size creatures, like siege lizards and mammoths.<br /> <br /> I'm talking about being able to turn into a Legendary Size version of your sprit shape, and for its stats to rival mammoths, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Mountainous Spirit Expression, right after Towering Beast Shape.<br /> <br /> You'll be able to make any of your forms giant, including the human and hybrid ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T08:27:58-08:00","id":1285905,"title":"","content":"Indeed, but Mountainous Spirit Expression was rubbish in 2nd ed, because it added a flat bonus to your spirit shape, so if your spirit shape had Strength and Stamina 1 (as many small animals do), the final stats you had were rather mediocre.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping this edition's version will be much stronger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T09:02:42-08:00","id":1285917,"title":"","content":"I want the Silver Pact to be a society - one where most everybody knows everybody else. That the Lunar signature stories are intertwined, even if they sometimes work at cross-purposes. That to be unknown to most of the Pact and also be a Lunar is a weird, young state of affairs. A loose sisterhood who understand that there is no line a member can cross that will completely exile them - save Chimerism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T13:13:24-08:00","id":1285995,"title":"","content":"Not really a want per say, but I'm curious what the size is going to be like. In previous editions all the splat books came in at around 250 pages, or thereabouts. For second edition things were more standardized and were all almost exactly 240. What Fire Has Wrought is currently 380, mostly because of the larger space needed.<br /> <br /> Aside from that there's chapter layout. After the intro chapter DB's had three separate fluff chapters since there's a lot of ground to cover, one for the realm, one for the great houses, and one for various outcaste groups. I'm picturing Lunar's only having the two, one for the silver pact and one for other assorted current affairs, and that after that things will follow the same pattern but with the artifacts chapter swapped for the animal chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","user":"Lionmanguy","date":". 02-08-2019, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T13:33:48-08:00","id":1286003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1285637-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1285995#post1285995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really a want per say, but I'm curious what the size is going to be like. In previous editions all the splat books came in at around 250 pages, or thereabouts. For second edition things were more standardized and were all almost exactly 240. What Fire Has Wrought is currently 380, mostly because of the larger space needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'll be roughly the same size as What Fire Has Wrought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T13:45:52-08:00","id":1286008,"title":"","content":"Oh. That's pleasant to hear, and only serves to make me even more curious.<br /> <br /> And I just remembered the other big thing I was curious about, what sort of stuff is going to get added to the companion. For DB's it was easy enough to fill, since there are several very big outcaste groups that don't have proper room to fit in the book itself like Prasad and the Forest Witches, but Lunars don't really have that. I'm wondering what's going to be in there aside from the standard bonus charms/animals/NPC write ups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T14:08:26-08:00","id":1286012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1285637-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1285917#post1285917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want the Silver Pact to be a society - one where most everybody knows everybody else.<br /> That to be unknown to most of the Pact and also be a Lunar is a weird, young state of affairs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm happy for it to be a society where all the Lunars around, say, the Dreaming Sea know each other.<br /> <br /> But it would seem weird to me for the 100 Lunars in the South to know all the 100 Lunars in the North, not to mention the rest of Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T19:41:21-08:00","id":1286071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1285637-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1285917#post1285917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want the Silver Pact to be a society - one where most everybody knows everybody else. That the Lunar signature stories are intertwined, even if they sometimes work at cross-purposes. That to be unknown to most of the Pact and also be a Lunar is a weird, young state of affairs. A loose sisterhood who understand that there is no line a member can cross that will completely exile them - save Chimerism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being a Chimera is apparently a legit lifestyle choice in 3e, not a sign of mounting madness and Wyld Addiction.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T20:52:45-08:00","id":1286087,"title":"","content":"I want beautiful charms that make everyone stand up and pay attention like &quot;Whoa, that's crazy! Lunars are cool!&quot; Things that are uniquely them and set them apart from other splats beyond just the changing into animals and people. I'm so damn hype for this to come out!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T06:14:22-08:00","id":1286163,"title":"","content":"As an answer to Friendless With Animals Approach, and owing to how Charisma Charms don't divide into Presence and Survival, I'm hoping for a Charisma Charm that convinces everyone around that you mean no harm, even when you're equipped for war and possibly dripping blood from a previous fight.<br /> <br /> Being a Charisma Charm and not a Manipulation Charm, it only works as long as you don't really don't mean to harm anyone, and fails the moment that you do.<br /> <br /> It does not protect you from hungry predators, though it will protect you against merely territorial ones.<br /> <br /> It does not by itself convince devout Immaculates seeing your true nature that you are harmless, as the very meaning of Anathema is one who is intrinsically harmful to the world, even if they don't mean to be in any particular moment.<br /> <br /> Similarly, if animals smell an infectious disease on you or sees that you are currently on fire, they don't that you mean no harm, you're very dangerous and they won't come near you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T06:32:45-08:00","id":1286167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1285637-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1286163#post1286163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Friendless With Animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Friendless, with animals. I wish this was a charm. <br /> <br /> Also that would be a cool lunar charm concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T06:37:12-08:00","id":1286169,"title":"","content":"That reminds me of Wearing Red to a Wedding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T06:47:21-08:00","id":1286171,"title":"","content":"That was a cool charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}